{"kind":"report","text":"CHECKER DECISION on 74d07139 (Stage 2 contract conflict): PATH 1, AMENDED - stay within the ratified constraints; no RuntimeID, canonicalization, or evaluator-confinement change; path 2 is rejected. Verification of the three claims: (c) calendar day is NOT blocked - daily-review already derives day_utc under the same confinement as $floor($number($event_time) / 86400000000000) (tailapps/daily-review/folds/normalize.jsonata line 125), so do that in the normalizer from the envelope time; do NOT add a tailapp.url.day_utc input. (a) correct - normalizer READ clauses bind only top-level envelope fields, so a normalizer cannot look up a prior row by observed_full, exclusion_id, or provider; but the original design note already allowed either one owning program, the normalizer OR a single fold, to materialize the tables, and the stage-1 note choice of the normalizer was an implementation detail, not operator policy. (b) exact re-parse is not required by policy; what matters is that the adapter cannot desynchronize host exclusions, which lowercase authority-prefix-plus-boundary validation achieves with admitted functions. RATIFIED STAGE 2 TOPOLOGY: the normalizer recognizes the three families (tailapp.url.observed / .exclusion / .reputation), validates required attributes, lowercases and validates the host by checking that $lowercase(observed_full) starts with http:// or https:// followed by the lowercase host and then either end-of-string or one of / : ? # (refuse otherwise, decision ineffective with a fact), derives day_utc as above, and emits ONE private event url_pipeline_event carrying event_family, observed_full, host, session/harness/tool/project when present, exclusion_id/kind/pattern/enabled, provider/checked_full/verdict/threat_types/provider_reference/error/checked_unix_nano/valid_until_unix_nano, the envelope time, and source position; ONE fold reads prior rows keyed by event fields (url_observations by observed_full; url_exclusions by exclusion_id; url_verdicts by observed_full+provider; url_pipeline_counts by day_utc+event_family) and is the SOLE WRITER of all four tables, seeding the built-in exclusion IDs only when its READ shows them absent; exports and the bounded due query with caller-bound :now_unix_nano unchanged. Everything else in #2741 stands. DOCS: in the same head, amend section 2 of notes/2026-08-31-url-reputation-stage-1-decisions.md to record this topology and the host-validation definition, citing this decision, so the ratified note stays truthful. Proceed with #2741 under this contract; address the review to checker."}